From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] Flush only the blocks of mapped memory the host does
 not already hold

A per-allocation shadow of the bytes last sent (caboose-bounded-memory/
flush_shadow.h) lets a flush send only the 256-byte blocks that changed within
pages the host already holds, up to 64 fragments per packet. Unmap and free
forget the host's copy; a successful invalidate refreshes it.
